Recommended approach:

## Main Rendering

Use a scalable SVG-based botanical rendering engine with carefully designed organic paths.

Use Bézier curves and variable-width branch silhouettes.

Use deterministic procedural layouts based on genealogical relationships.

Consider a Canvas or WebGL layer for decorative leaves and atmospheric effects if necessary.

Use separate rendering layers:

### Layer A — Atmosphere

Background, sunlight, distant foliage, subtle environment.

### Layer B — Botanical Structure

Main trunk, major branches, secondary branches, twigs.

### Layer C — Leaves

Decorative foliage and meaningful individual markers.

### Layer D — Interactive Labels

Arabic names and accessible interactive targets.

### Layer E — Interaction

Selection indicators, editing controls, contextual menus, profile panels.

### Layer F — Camera

Zoom, pan, focus, and animated navigation.

